      {
        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 4 data columns across 1 file.",
          "**A codebook was found and parsed (8 variable definitions), but its variable names do not match the data columns, so the documentation could not be linked automatically (only 0% of columns matched). For example, the codebook documents `neo1`, `neo2`, `neo3` while the data has `id`, `neoImagination`, `neoAnxiety`. This often means the data holds computed scores or subscales while the codebook lists the underlying items. To make the codebook usable automatically, document variables under the exact names used in the data file (one row per data column), with a label and, for rating items, the response scale.**",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"id\", \"neoAnxiety\", \"neoImagination\", \n\"neoWarmth\"), Documented = c(\"no\", \"no\", \"no\", \"no\"), Label = c(NA_character_, \nNA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(NA_character_, \nNA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_), Source = c(NA_character_, \nNA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_), Status = c(\"unlabelled\", \n\"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\")), row.names = c(NA, \n4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Documented but Unused Variables\n\n8 documented variables were not matched to any data column.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Variable = c(\"neo1\", \"neo2\", \"neo3\", \"neo4\", \"neo5\", \n\"neo6\", \"neo7\", \"neo8\"), Label = c(\"NEO item 1\", \"NEO item 2\", \n\"NEO item 3\", \"NEO item 4\", \"NEO item 5\", \"NEO item 6\", \"NEO item 7\", \n\"NEO item 8\"), Source = c(\"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \n\"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \n\"codebook.csv\")), row.names = c(NA, 8L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Scales",
          "Scale naming from the manuscript needs an LLM (enable with `llm_use(TRUE)`); the dictionary rules matcher still names instruments whose abbreviation matches a known scale."
        ]
      },
